<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Base application theme — edge-to-edge, dark-first ("Undertow").
      This XML theme only governs the window BEFORE Compose takes over:
      windowBackground is the branded launch drawable (ink background, logo
      mark centred on API 23+; flat ink on API 21-22, where a layer-list item
      cannot carry gravity) so a cold start shows a loading screen instead of
      flat black, and the nav-drawer flash stays the same ink the first frame
      paints. System bars stay transparent (enableEdgeToEdge in MainActivity)
      and their icon contrast is handled by the dark background.

      Only attributes that exist at minSdk 21 belong here. `android:windowLightStatusBar`
      (API 23) lives in values-v23 and `android:windowLayoutInDisplayCutoutMode` (API 27) in
      values-v27; below their introduction level the platform ignored them anyway, so the
      rendered window is unchanged on every device. A version-qualified folder REPLACES this
      style wholesale rather than merging into it, which is why each override repeats the three
      items below — trimming them there to avoid the duplication is what would actually change
      behavior. That split is also what `lintDebug`'s NewApi check asks for; keeping it in one
      file needs an annotation suppression, which would silence the check for every real case too.

      Only attributes that exist at minSdk 21 belong here. `android:windowLightStatusBar`
      (API 23) lives in values-v23 and `android:windowLayoutInDisplayCutoutMode` (API 27) in
      values-v27; below their introduction level the platform ignored them anyway, so the
      rendered window is unchanged on every device. A version-qualified folder REPLACES this
      style wholesale rather than merging into it, which is why each override repeats the three
      items below — trimming them there to avoid the duplication is what would actually change
      behavior. That split is also what `lintDebug`'s NewApi check asks for; keeping it in one
      file needs an annotation suppression, which would silence the check for every real case too.

      BRAND: @color/radd_ink_950 is NOT declared in res/values/colors.xml any
      more — it is generated at build time from [resources.colors] in
      /brand.properties (see app/build.gradle.kts), and RaddInk950 itself reads
      [colors.dark] background from the same file. The style NAME stays literal
      because AndroidManifest.xml must reference a real resource name.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.RaddStream" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/launch_background</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">#00000000</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">#00000000</item>
        <!--
          AppCompat theme colors. The platform Material parent defines
          android:colorPrimary but NOT the AppCompat colorPrimary attribute, so
          any AppCompat widget that resolves it (MediaRouteButton does, in
          MediaRouterThemeHelper.getControllerColor) got 0 — transparent — and
          ColorUtils.calculateContrast threw IllegalArgumentException
          ("background can not be translucent: #0"), crashing every detail
          screen that composed the Cast button (Robo v11, 3 crashes). These
          are opaque brand colors, so the resolution can never be 0 again.
          Like the items above, they must be repeated in values-v23 and
          values-v27, whose styles replace this one wholesale.
        -->
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/radd_current</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/radd_current_700</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/radd_current</item>
    </style>
</resources>
